# Database migrations

Run commands from the repository root unless noted otherwise.

Start PostgreSQL:

```powershell
docker compose up -d db
```

Apply migrations from the `backend` directory:

```powershell
cd backend
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head
```

Alembic reads `DATABASE_URL` from `backend\.env`. Use `backend\.env.example`
as the template for local configuration.

To remove the schema created by the initial migration, run
`.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic downgrade base` from `backend`.
This drops the OpsDesk tables and their data.